{%- comment -%}
  Private to Product card; explicitly targeted there and nowhere else.

  Product card — one option control on the card itself.

  Picking a value moves the caption, the price and what goes in the bag — and
  deliberately *not* the photograph. A card can show one option axis without
  pretending it has resolved every other option on a complex product.

  Every control is a **real link** to the piece at that value, so a pick works
  without scripting — it simply navigates — and each value's price markup is
  rendered onto the link by Liquid, so a pick costs no request and no
  arithmetic in the browser. (The design uses a `<button>`; a button without
  script does nothing, and the theme's rule is that nothing is load-bearing
  without scripting.)

  The chosen value is live control state, so it belongs here rather than in a
  second Product text block. It stays independently styled in `.card__meta`,
  and `theme.js` updates it from the selected link's `data-option-meta` value.

  The merchant can leave the target on Auto, enter one of the shop's own option
  names, or nominate Shopify option 1, 2 or 3. No catalogue names are built
  into the theme. A name or position the product does not have renders nothing.

  Every value publishes both its option index and the complete variant it
  resolves to. That lets `theme.js` keep another Option control, the price,
  Quick view and the add action on the same variant even when two different
  option axes are shown on one card.

  **Swatches paint from the option value's native Shopify swatch and from
  nowhere else.** Auto uses swatches when this option carries them and written
  values otherwise. A forced swatch with no configured paint keeps its hairline
  and accessible name, so it stays pickable and announced. Never hardcode a
  table of values here.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
  capture card_option_raw
    render 'card-option', product: product, source_mode: block.settings.target_by, source_name: block.settings.option_name, source: block.settings.option_position
  endcapture
  assign card_option = card_option_raw | strip | split: '||'
  assign opt_index = card_option[0] | plus: 0
  assign selected_value = ''
  if card_option.size > 2
    assign selected_value = card_option[1]
  endif

  assign card_option_drop = blank
  if opt_index >= 0
    for option in product.options_with_values
      if forloop.index0 == opt_index
        assign card_option_drop = option
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    **The order is the merchant's own.** Values come straight from the selected
    option in Shopify admin. The theme neither sorts them alphabetically nor
    carries a catalogue-specific value table.

    They stay `product_option_value` drops rather than being flattened to
    strings, which is what carries a merchant's native Shopify swatch — the
    round trip through `split` was why the swatch had to be looked up again.
  endcomment
  assign ordered_values = card_option_drop.values

  assign option_has_swatches = false
  for value in ordered_values
    if value.swatch.color != blank or value.swatch.image != blank
      assign option_has_swatches = true
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign is_pills = false
  if block.settings.control == 'pills'
    assign is_pills = true
  elsif block.settings.control == 'auto'
    unless option_has_swatches
      assign is_pills = true
    endunless
  endif

  comment
    Round or square, and it is one declaration rather than a second dot. The
    radius is published as `--swatch-radius`, which `.swatch-dot` reads with a
    `50%` fallback — so the dot is round wherever nothing says otherwise, which
    is every other place it is drawn (the quick view, the product page).
  endcomment
  assign swatch_radius = '50%'
  if block.settings.swatch_shape == 'square'
    assign swatch_radius = 'var(--radius-base, 0)'
  endif
-%}

{%- if card_option_drop != blank -%}
  <div
    class="card__option-control"
    data-card-option-control
    data-option-index="{{ opt_index }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <span class="card__meta" data-card-meta>{{ selected_value }}</span>

    <div
      class="{% if is_pills %}card__pills{% else %}card__swatches{% endif %}"
      {% unless is_pills %}data-card-swatches style="--swatch-radius: {{ swatch_radius }};"{% endunless %}
    >
      {%- for value in ordered_values -%}
      {%- liquid
        comment
          Keep Shopify's merchant-defined variant order: the first available
          variant carrying this value, then the first matching variant if the
          whole value is sold out. Multi-option products use this id only to
          preselect Quick View; they are never silently added from the card.

          This is `card-option.liquid`'s rule applied per value rather than to
          the selected one, which is why it is written out here — the snippet
          answers for the card's current state, and the row has to answer for
          every state the card could be put into.
        endcomment
        assign chosen = blank
        assign first_any = blank
        for variant in product.variants
          if variant.options[opt_index] == value
            if first_any == blank
              assign first_any = variant
            endif
            if chosen == blank and variant.available
              assign chosen = variant
            endif
          endif
        endfor
        if chosen == blank
          assign chosen = first_any
        endif

        assign is_selected = false
        if value == selected_value
          assign is_selected = true
        endif

      -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The price markup a pick writes into `[data-card-price]`. It carries the
        figure and nothing else: `theme.js` replaces that element's whole
        `innerHTML`, and anything beside the price — a note, a unit — is a
        sibling block out of its reach.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture value_price_html -%}
        {%- if chosen.compare_at_price > chosen.price -%}
          <s>{{ chosen.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
        {%- endif -%}
        {{- chosen.price | money -}}
      {%- endcapture -%}

        <a
          class="{% if is_pills %}card__pill{% else %}card__swatch{% endif %}{% if is_selected %} is-selected{% endif %}"
          href="{{ product.url }}?variant={{ chosen.id }}"
          data-card-option
          data-option-value="{{ value | escape }}"
          data-option-index="{{ opt_index }}"
          data-option-values="{{ chosen.options | json | escape }}"
          data-option-id="{{ chosen.id }}"
          data-option-available="{{ chosen.available }}"
          data-option-meta="{{ value | escape }}"
          data-option-price="{{ value_price_html | escape }}"
          {% unless is_pills %}data-tip="{{ value | escape }}"{% endunless %}
          aria-label="{{ value | escape }}"
          aria-current="{% if is_selected %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
          {% if is_pills == false and forloop.index0 >= 3 %}hidden{% endif %}
        >
        {%- comment -%}
          `selected` is deliberately not passed to the dot. The wrapping link
          carries the state and `.card__swatch.is-selected .swatch-dot` draws
          the ring from it, so there is one source of truth. Marking the dot as
          well left two rings after a pick: the script moves the class on the
          link and never on the dot.
        {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if is_pills -%}
            {{- value -}}
          {%- else -%}
            {% render 'option-swatch', option_value: value, size: 80 %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </a>
      {%- endfor -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The design's "+N". Before a width is known it shows three —
      `else if (!avail) n = Math.min(keys.length, 3)` — so that is what Liquid
      renders, and the script re-fits once it can measure. Pills wrap instead of
      clipping, so they need none of it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- unless is_pills -%}
        {%- assign value_total = ordered_values.size -%}
        <span
          class="card__swatch-more"
          data-card-swatch-more
          {% if value_total <= 3 %}hidden{% endif %}
        >{% if value_total > 3 %}+{{ value_total | minus: 3 }}{% endif %}</span>
      {%- endunless -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "target_by",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.target_by.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.target_by.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "auto", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.target_by.auto" },
        { "value": "name", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.target_by.name" },
        { "value": "position", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.target_by.position" }
      ],
      "default": "auto"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "option_name",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.option_name.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.option_name.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.target_by == 'name' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "option_position",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.option_position.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.option_position.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.target_by == 'position' }}",
      "options": [
        { "value": "1", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.option_position.first" },
        { "value": "2", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.option_position.second" },
        { "value": "3", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.option_position.third" }
      ],
      "default": "1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "control",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.control.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.control.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "auto", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.control.auto" },
        { "value": "swatches", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.control.swatches" },
        { "value": "pills", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.control.pills" }
      ],
      "default": "auto"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "swatch_shape",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.swatch_shape.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.control == 'swatches' }}",
      "options": [
        { "value": "round", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.swatch_shape.round" },
        { "value": "square", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.swatch_shape.square" }
      ],
      "default": "round"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.product_card_variants.name",
      "settings": {
        "target_by": "auto",
        "control": "auto",
        "swatch_shape": "round"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
